1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,752
The minimum payment is the most expensive button

2
00:00:02,792 --> 00:00:03,975
in your card app.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,578
On a €3,000 card, the minimum starts at €60 a month.

4
00:00:08,618 --> 00:00:09,860
Keep paying just that,

5
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,782
and it takes about nine years.

6
00:00:11,822 --> 00:00:15,161
Pay €150, and it's gone in about two.

7
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,054
That's not because you're bad with money.

8
00:00:18,094 --> 00:00:19,999
The lower the minimum, the longer you pay,

9
00:00:20,039 --> 00:00:21,762
and the more the lender earns.

10
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:24,997
Here's how to escape it, in six steps.

11
00:00:26,167 --> 00:00:28,723
One. Put it all on one page.

12
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:31,071
Write down every debt:

13
00:00:31,111 --> 00:00:32,828
how much you owe, the interest rate,

14
00:00:32,868 --> 00:00:34,304
and the minimum payment.

15
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,305
Include everything:

16
00:00:36,345 --> 00:00:38,566
cards, store credit, buy now pay later,

17
00:00:38,606 --> 00:00:41,167
car loans, even money you owe friends.

18
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:44,913
Most people have never seen the total in one place.

19
00:00:44,953 --> 00:00:46,732
It's scary for ten minutes.

20
00:00:46,772 --> 00:00:48,168
Then it's a plan.

21
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,335
And if it feels like too much,

22
00:00:50,375 --> 00:00:53,129
free debt advice exists in most countries.

23
00:00:53,169 --> 00:00:54,183
Use it.

24
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,989
Two. Escape the minimum payment.

25
00:00:58,467 --> 00:01:02,285
Back to that €3,000 card, at 20% a year.

26
00:01:02,325 --> 00:01:04,007
At a fixed €60 a month,

27
00:01:04,047 --> 00:01:07,374
you pay around €3,500 in interest.

28
00:01:07,414 --> 00:01:09,130
More than the debt itself.

29
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,246
And many real minimums are

30
00:01:11,286 --> 00:01:12,658
just a slice of what you owe,

31
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:14,061
like 2%.

32
00:01:14,101 --> 00:01:16,554
As the debt shrinks, the payment shrinks too.

33
00:01:16,594 --> 00:01:17,563
Pay only that,

34
00:01:17,603 --> 00:01:20,283
and the same card can take over thirty years,

35
00:01:20,323 --> 00:01:23,110
and about €11,000 in interest.

36
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:26,201
The rules vary by country, so check yours.

37
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:31,772
At €150 a month, it's about €680 of interest,

38
00:01:31,812 --> 00:01:33,851
and two years instead of nine.

39
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,348
Same debt. Same rate.

40
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:38,406
Seven years of your life back.

41
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,629
Three. Pick an order.

42
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,795
The avalanche: pay the minimum on everything,

43
00:01:44,835 --> 00:01:46,369
and throw every extra euro

44
00:01:46,409 --> 00:01:48,628
at the highest interest rate first.

45
00:01:48,668 --> 00:01:51,079
Mathematically, it saves the most.

46
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:52,238
The snowball:

47
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:54,127
smallest balance first.

48
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:55,638
You close accounts quickly,

49
00:01:55,678 --> 00:01:57,507
and each win keeps you going.

50
00:01:58,167 --> 00:02:01,112
Say you have €300 a month for all three.

51
00:02:01,152 --> 00:02:04,341
The avalanche saves about €80 in interest.

52
00:02:04,381 --> 00:02:07,007
The snowball clears its first debt in five months,

53
00:02:07,047 --> 00:02:08,369
instead of twelve.

54
00:02:08,409 --> 00:02:10,497
Both are done in about two years.

55
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,442
In one study of about six thousand people

56
00:02:13,482 --> 00:02:14,540
in a debt programme,

57
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:16,196
those who cleared small accounts

58
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,391
first were more likely

59
00:02:17,431 --> 00:02:19,127
to clear all of their debt.

60
00:02:19,167 --> 00:02:21,643
So if the rates are similar, start small.

61
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:23,073
If one rate is much higher,

62
00:02:23,113 --> 00:02:25,266
like this card, kill that one first.

63
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:28,870
Four. One debt at a time.

64
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:31,242
Spreading your extra money thinly

65
00:02:31,282 --> 00:02:33,045
across every debt feels fair.

66
00:02:33,085 --> 00:02:35,006
But then nothing seems to move.

67
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:36,855
Researchers found that people

68
00:02:36,895 --> 00:02:38,461
who focused their repayments

69
00:02:38,501 --> 00:02:40,953
on one account at a time felt more progress,

70
00:02:40,993 --> 00:02:42,733
and paid more aggressively.

71
00:02:43,367 --> 00:02:44,242
When one is gone,

72
00:02:44,282 --> 00:02:46,486
roll its whole payment into the next.

73
00:02:46,526 --> 00:02:49,110
Every payoff makes the next one faster.

74
00:02:50,233 --> 00:02:52,826
Five. Make the interest smaller.

75
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:55,481
Ask your lender for a lower rate.

76
00:02:55,521 --> 00:02:58,500
It doesn't always work, but it costs nothing to ask.

77
00:02:59,233 --> 00:03:01,343
A consolidation loan can help too,

78
00:03:01,383 --> 00:03:04,035
but only if you stop using the old cards.

79
00:03:04,075 --> 00:03:05,805
And check the total cost:

80
00:03:05,845 --> 00:03:07,933
a longer loan can cost more overall,

81
00:03:07,973 --> 00:03:09,562
even at a lower rate.

82
00:03:10,267 --> 00:03:12,109
Even a few points matter.

83
00:03:12,149 --> 00:03:16,965
On €3,000, going from 20% to 10% cuts the interest

84
00:03:17,005 --> 00:03:21,108
from about €600 a year to about €300.

85
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:24,569
Six. Don't refill the card.

86
00:03:25,267 --> 00:03:28,337
Keep a small emergency fund, even €500,

87
00:03:28,377 --> 00:03:31,089
so the next surprise doesn't go straight back

88
00:03:31,129 --> 00:03:33,773
on the card. And when your last debt is gone,

89
00:03:33,813 --> 00:03:36,512
keep paying the same amount, into your savings.

90
00:03:37,267 --> 00:03:38,681
And keep it visible:

91
00:03:38,721 --> 00:03:39,852
a list on the fridge,

92
00:03:39,892 --> 00:03:41,812
crossed out one line at a time.

93
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:44,296
Final message.

94
00:03:45,033 --> 00:03:46,979
Debt isn't a character flaw.

95
00:03:47,019 --> 00:03:48,118
It's a maths problem,

96
00:03:48,158 --> 00:03:50,112
and maths problems can be solved.

97
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:53,399
List it. Pay more than the minimum.

98
00:03:53,439 --> 00:03:54,648
Pick an order.

99
00:03:54,688 --> 00:03:56,026
One at a time.

100
00:03:56,066 --> 00:03:57,409
Lower the rate.

101
00:03:57,449 --> 00:03:58,845
Don't refill it.

102
00:03:59,033 --> 00:04:00,536
That's the whole plan.

103
00:04:00,576 --> 00:04:02,934
Screenshot it, and stick it on the fridge.

104
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:06,456
This is education, not financial advice.

105
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:08,125
If debt feels unmanageable,

106
00:04:08,165 --> 00:04:11,054
many countries have free debt advice services.

107
00:04:11,094 --> 00:04:12,861
If this helped, subscribe.

108
00:04:12,901 --> 00:04:16,455
Next up: how to invest your first thousand euros.
